<!-- ============ SECTION 1 ============ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h1>1. Problem Statement</h1>

<p>When a user uploaded a new CSV file with updated sales data, the <strong>Dashboard</strong> and <strong>Forecasts</strong> pages continued to display old forecast data from the previous dataset. The user had no indication that the displayed forecasts were outdated.</p>

<div class="warning-box">
  <strong>⚠️ User Impact:</strong> Users would make business decisions based on forecasts they believed were for their new data, but were actually from their previous CSV upload.
</div>

<h3>Example Scenario</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>Step</th><th>User Action</th><th>Result</th><th>Status</th></tr>
  <tr><td>1</td><td>Upload <code>sales_january.csv</code></td><td>Data saved to MongoDB</td><td>✅ OK</td></tr>
  <tr><td>2</td><td>Generate Forecasts</td><td>January predictions created</td><td>✅ OK</td></tr>
  <tr><td>3</td><td>Upload <code>sales_february.csv</code></td><td>New data saved</td><td>✅ OK</td></tr>
  <tr><td>4</td><td>Navigate to Dashboard</td><td><strong>Still shows January forecasts!</strong></td><td>❌ BUG</td></tr>
  <tr><td>5</td><td>Navigate to Forecasts page</td><td><strong>Old forecast cards with no warning</strong></td><td>❌ BUG</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Root Causes Identified</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>No staleness tracking:</strong> Forecast documents in MongoDB had no way to indicate they were outdated relative to newer sales data.</li>
  <li><strong>No auto-regeneration:</strong> After upload, forecasts were not automatically regenerated — user had to manually click "Generate Forecasts".</li>
  <li><strong>Async cache busting:</strong> Redis cache was cleared using <code>setImmediate()</code> (fire-and-forget), causing a race condition where the client could navigate and still receive cached old data.</li>
  <li><strong>No UI indication:</strong> Neither the Dashboard nor Forecasts page showed any warning when forecast data was outdated.</li>
</ol>

<!-- ============ SECTION 2 ============ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h1>2. Solution Overview</h1>

<p>The fix uses a <strong>3-layer approach</strong>:</p>

<table>
  <tr><th>Layer</th><th>What It Does</th><th>Where</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>1. Mark Stale</strong></td>
    <td>When new CSV is uploaded, all existing forecasts are marked <code>isStale: true</code></td>
    <td>Server (upload route)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>2. Auto-Generate</strong></td>
    <td>Forecast regeneration starts automatically in the background after upload</td>
    <td>Server (forecastRunner)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>3. Live UI Feedback</strong></td>
    <td>Progress cards, warning banners, and stale badges shown on Dashboard &amp; Forecasts pages</td>
    <td>Client (React components)</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<!-- ============ SECTION 3 ============ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h1>3. Backend Changes</h1>

<h2>3.1 Forecast Model</h2>
<h4>File: <code>server/models/Forecast.js</code> <span class="badge badge-modified">MODIFIED</span></h4>

<p>Added a new boolean field <code>isStale</code> to the Mongoose schema:</p>
<pre>isStale: { type: Boolean, default: false }</pre>

<div class="highlight-box">
  <strong>Purpose:</strong> This field acts as a flag. When <code>true</code>, it tells the frontend that this forecast was generated from an older dataset and should be displayed with a warning.
</div>

<h2>3.2 Forecast Runner Service</h2>
<h4>File: <code>server/services/forecastRunner.js</code> <span class="badge badge-modified">MODIFIED</span></h4>

<p><strong>Changes made:</strong></p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Imported <code>forecastTracker</code></strong> — for tracking background job progress</li>
  <li><strong>Set <code>isStale: false</code> in <code>processProduct()</code></strong> — when a forecast is freshly generated, it is marked as not stale</li>
  <li><strong>Created <code>triggerForecastGeneration(userId, opts)</code></strong> — a new exported helper function that:
    <ul>
      <li>Checks if a job is already running</li>
      <li>Validates that enough sales data exists (minimum 10 records)</li>
      <li>Finds eligible products (minimum 5 records per product)</li>
      <li>Initializes the progress tracker</li>
      <li>Starts background generation with progress callbacks</li>
      <li>Returns immediate status: <code>started</code>, <code>already_running</code>, or <code>skipped</code></li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<div class="highlight-box">
  <strong>Why a helper function?</strong> Both the upload route (auto-trigger) and the forecast route (manual trigger) need the same validation and generation logic. Extracting it into a shared function avoids code duplication (~80 lines of duplicated code removed from forecast route).
</div>

<h2>3.3 Forecast Routes</h2>
<h4>File: <code>server/routes/forecast.js</code> <span class="badge badge-modified">MODIFIED</span></h4>

<p><strong>Changes made:</strong></p>
<ol>
  <li>Imported <code>triggerForecastGeneration</code> from forecastRunner</li>
  <li>Simplified <code>POST /generate</code> endpoint — now calls the helper instead of duplicating logic</li>
</ol>

<p><strong>Before (98 lines):</strong></p>
<pre>router.post('/generate', requireAuth, asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  // ... 80+ lines of validation, eligibility, tracker init, background trigger
}));</pre>

<p><strong>After (20 lines):</strong></p>
<pre>router.post('/generate', requireAuth, asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  const result = await triggerForecastGeneration(userId, { forecastDays, model, trigger: 'manual' });
  if (result.status === 'already_running') return res.status(400).json({ error: '...' });
  if (result.status === 'skipped') return res.status(400).json({ error: result.reason });
  res.json({ status: 'started', message: 'Forecast generation started.' });
}));</pre>

<h2>3.4 Upload Routes</h2>
<h4>File: <code>server/routes/upload.js</code> <span class="badge badge-modified">MODIFIED</span></h4>

<p>This is the <strong>most critical change</strong>. After a successful CSV upload, three new operations happen:</p>

<table>
  <tr><th>#</th><th>Operation</th><th>Code</th><th>Timing</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>1</td>
    <td>Mark all forecasts as stale</td>
    <td><code>Forecast.updateMany({ userId }, { isStale: true })</code></td>
    <td>Synchronous (before response)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>2</td>
    <td>Bust Redis cache</td>
    <td><code>cache.delPattern('sales:...', 'inventory:...', 'forecast:...')</code></td>
    <td>Synchronous (before response)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>3</td>
    <td>Auto-trigger forecast generation</td>
    <td><code>triggerForecastGeneration(userId, { model, trigger: 'upload' })</code></td>
    <td>Background (setImmediate)</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<div class="success-box">
  <strong>Key improvement:</strong> Cache busting was moved from <code>setImmediate</code> (async/fire-and-forget) to <code>await</code> (synchronous). This eliminates the race condition where the client navigates to the Dashboard and receives cached stale data.
</div>

<!-- ============ SECTION 4 ============ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h1>4. Frontend Changes</h1>

<h2>4.1 ForecastProgress Component</h2>
<h4>File: <code>client/src/components/ForecastProgress/ForecastProgress.jsx</code> <span class="badge badge-new">NEW</span></h4>
<h4>File: <code>client/src/components/ForecastProgress/ForecastProgress.css</code> <span class="badge badge-new">NEW</span></h4>

<p>A reusable React component that displays a live progress card when a forecast generation job is active. Features:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Pulse icon animation</strong> — visual indicator that processing is active</li>
  <li><strong>Elapsed time</strong> — how long the job has been running</li>
  <li><strong>Estimated remaining time</strong> — calculated from average time per product</li>
  <li><strong>Progress bar</strong> — gradient fill showing percentage complete</li>
  <li><strong>Rotating slideshow</strong> (every 3 seconds) — alternates between:
    <ul>
      <li>Overall progress percentage</li>
      <li>Current product being forecasted</li>
      <li>Time estimate details</li>
      <li>Active ML engines list</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>4.2 StaleBanner Component</h2>
<h4>File: <code>client/src/components/StaleBanner/StaleBanner.jsx</code> <span class="badge badge-new">NEW</span></h4>
<h4>File: <code>client/src/components/StaleBanner/StaleBanner.css</code> <span class="badge badge-new">NEW</span></h4>

<p>A warning banner that appears in two states:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>State</th><th>Message</th><th>Appearance</th><th>Action Button</th></tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Generating</td>
    <td>"Forecast updates in progress. Previous estimations are shown below."</td>
    <td>Purple/indigo theme</td>
    <td>None (wait)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Stale (not generating)</td>
    <td>"New data uploaded. Forecasts below are based on previous dataset."</td>
    <td>Amber/warning theme</td>
    <td>"Regenerate Now" button</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>4.3 Dashboard Page</h2>
<h4>File: <code>client/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx</code> <span class="badge badge-modified">MODIFIED</span></h4>
<h4>File: <code>client/src/pages/Dashboard.css</code> <span class="badge badge-modified">MODIFIED</span></h4>

<p><strong>New functionality added:</strong></p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Status polling:</strong> On page load, checks <code>/api/forecast/status</code>. If a job is running, polls every 2 seconds until complete.</li>
  <li><strong>Progress card:</strong> <code>&lt;ForecastProgress&gt;</code> rendered at the top of the page when a job is active.</li>
  <li><strong>Stale banner:</strong> <code>&lt;StaleBanner&gt;</code> shown when forecasts are stale or generation is in progress.</li>
  <li><strong>Revenue Overview chart:</strong> Gets a "Stale" or "Updating..." pill badge and dimmed content when data is outdated.</li>
  <li><strong>Reorder Recommendations table:</strong> Same stale treatment as Revenue chart.</li>
  <li><strong>Auto-refresh:</strong> When generation completes, forecasts are automatically reloaded and all warnings disappear.</li>
</ol>

<h2>4.4 Forecasts Page</h2>
<h4>File: <code>client/src/pages/Forecasts.jsx</code> <span class="badge badge-modified">MODIFIED</span></h4>
<h4>File: <code>client/src/pages/Forecasts.css</code> <span class="badge badge-modified">MODIFIED</span></h4>

<p><strong>Changes made:</strong></p>
<ol>
  <li>Replaced inline progress card (50+ lines) with reusable <code>&lt;ForecastProgress&gt;</code></li>
  <li>Added <code>&lt;StaleBanner&gt;</code> below the page header</li>
  <li>Each forecast card shows a "Stale" badge when <code>forecast.isStale === true</code></li>
  <li>Stale cards get amber border and reduced opacity</li>
</ol>

<!-- ============ SECTION 5 ============ -->
<div class="page-break"></div>
<h1>5. Complete Data Flow</h1>

<div class="flow-diagram">
User uploads new CSV
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Upload Route (upload.js)           │
│  1. Parse &amp; save sales rows        │
│  2. Update inventory                │
│  3. Mark forecasts isStale = true   │
│  4. Bust Redis cache (synchronous)  │
│  5. Send success response to client │
│  6. Auto-trigger generation (bg)    │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Dashboard / Forecasts Page         │
│  1. Loads page → fetches forecasts  │
│  2. Detects isStale on forecasts    │
│  3. Polls /api/forecast/status      │
│  4. Shows ForecastProgress card     │
│  5. Shows StaleBanner warning       │
│  6. Dims forecast-dependent widgets │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
        │
        ▼ (generation completes)
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Automatic Cleanup                  │
│  1. Forecasts reloaded (fresh data) │
│  2. isStale = false on all new ones │
│  3. Banners &amp; badges disappear     │
│  4. Success toast notification      │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
</div>

